253 0 obj
<<
/Type /StructElem
/S /P
/P 83 0 R
/E (The ERD uses Chen notation. Rectangles represent entities; diamonds represent relationships; ovals represent attributes. Underlined attributes are primary keys. Double ovals represent multivalued attributes, dashed ovals represent derived attributes, and double lines indicate total participation. Cardinality labels \(1, N, M\) are read from the opposite entity's perspective, following the course guidance. The database is organized into three logical areas: \(1\) exams, students, consent and testing-center arrangements; \(2\) examsession monitoring, recordings, identity checks, proctor actions and human review; and \(3\) academic-integrity cases, student responses, appeals, notifications and committee decisions.)
/Pg 17 0 R
/K [5]
>>
